  "findings": [
    "Original128B producer requires NUM_MMA_KV*4 divisible by NUM_WARPS_Q;64B requires*2. The genericFP8*2 guard is conservative for128B, not the exact original row coverage requirement.",
    "All4warp layouts and current finite64/64,64/128,128/128,256/256 domains enumerated.128B K/V LDMATRIX row addresses stay within the same16-row block for MMA_KV1; shuffles stay within the32-lane warp.",
    "The original storage-only dispatch budget uses compressed1-byte KV payload although score and PV math widen to2-byte Q type and retain float accumulators. This can enlarge per-warp KV work relative to the original native16bit path.",
    "A native16bit working-set bound borrows the original16bit footprint rule solely to bound FP8 MMA work; physical smem remains compressed. This is a selection bound, not a claimed register byte count."
  ],
  "finite_fix": [
    "Use exact original128B*4 row divisibility and corresponding min valid tile only for FP8; retain64B*2 and allFP4 restrictions.",
    "In three original dispatchers cap FP8 MMA_KV by the existing native16bit footprint budget, clamped to the exact valid minimum; retain actual physical smem cap, original register cap and dispatch macro.",
    "No datatype-specific tile trials, shape-specific tuning, planner or mathematical primitive changes."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Source/math-layout audit and actual attribute projection only; no product implementation or performance PASS.",
    "New smaller valid specializations require actual17math/device and codegen; runtime dispatch identity and original qualified P1 remain necessary."
